.TH LDAP-PROBE 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ldap-probe \- anonymous LDAPS rootDSE diagnostic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ldap-probe
.BI --uri " ldaps://HOST[:PORT]"
.RB [ --timeout " 1..10]"
.br
.B ldap-probe
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an optional ldapsearch binary (without a shell), with an anonymous
LDAPv3 bind and rootDSE base-scope query. Requests supportedLDAPVersion,
namingContexts and defaultNamingContext; never modifies directory entries.
A successful query is not proof that NSS LDAP lookups work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --uri " LDAPS-URI"
Only ldaps://HOST[:PORT] or bracketed IPv6 is allowed; no credentials,
ldap://, free LDAP filters or URL query components.
.TP
.BI --timeout " 1..10"
Native LDAP client network timeout in seconds; default 5.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH SECURITY
For OpenLDAP, forces LDAPTLS_REQCERT=demand. Do not bypass certificate
validation. Only probe authorized servers. Output is unverified remote LDIF.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 client query succeeded; 1 query failed; 2 bad arguments; 3 missing client
or other prerequisite/internal failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
ldapsearch(1), ldap.conf(5)
